	(gr_text_box "Welcome to de-link, the open-source ESP32 reading/devkit platform. \n\nAll components will be on the back of this board, maximizing    .       cost and simplicity for DIY. Please build and repair as you please!\n\n.       This board mainly supports the GDEQ426T82 display variant, but it can be repurposed for most other GoodDisplay / Waveshare branded SPI e-paper displays. The buttons can be manually placed elsewhere by connecting to the marked positions of each labeled side-mounted switch. The other side of these normally-open switches is ground, with the exception being the power button which is normally open between GPIO3 and 3v3. \n\nYou may also access the header of LED pins, unused GPIO, UART, and GND/3v3 via 10-pin accessory connected on the top of the other side."
		(start 53.795 85.725)
		(end 94.795 118.685)
		(margins 1.0025 1.0025 1.0025 1.0025)
		(layer "F.SilkS")
		(uuid "2d362b9a-efbd-4666-bbb6-a5d15efd9713")
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Roboto")
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(border yes)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(render_cache "Welcome to de-link, the open-source ESP32 reading/devkit\nplatform.\n\nAll components will be on the back of this board, maximizing\n.       cost and simplicity for DIY. Please build and repair as you\nplease!\n\n.       This board mainly supports the GDEQ426T82 display\nvariant, but it can be repurposed for most other GoodDisplay /\nWaveshare branded SPI e-paper displays. The buttons can be\nmanually placed elsewhere by connecting to the marked\npositions of each labeled side-mounted switch. The other side\nof these normally-open switches is ground, with the exception\nbeing the power button which is normally open between GPIO3\nand 3v3.\n\nYou may also access the header of LED pins, unused GPIO,\nUART, and GND/3v3 via 10-pin accessory connected on the top\nof the other side."
			0
